“oscillator” is always being drawn in polar coordinates:

angle = (i/bufferLength)*2π
r = waveRadius + offset
x = cx + cos(angle)*r
y = cy + sin(angle)*r


So it can’t ever start as a straight oscilloscope line — it starts life as a ring.

What you want is a morph:

Mode 0 (start): classic oscilloscope line (left→right sine wave)

Mode 1 (modulated): the ring/loop form (circle-ish)

And you blend between them with a modulation amount m (0..1), driven by bass/arousal/whatever

Drop-in change (only touches LiveVisualizer.tsx)

Replace your LAYER 4 block with this morph version.

1) Add helpers near the top of render()

Right before // --- LAYER 4: Central Oscillating Core --- add:

const clamp01 = (x: number) => Math.max(0, Math.min(1, x));

// “Modulation” controls how much the line turns into a loop.
// Start mostly line; become loop when arousal + bass rise.
const m = clamp01(arousal * 0.85 + bass * 0.65);

// Core size / amplitude
const coreRadius = 55 + bass * 25;
const amp = 35 + bass * 55; // line amplitude

2) Replace LAYER 4 with a blended path

Replace your current ring code with:

// --- LAYER 4: Central Oscillator (Line -> Loop Morph) ---
ctx.beginPath();

// A little time phase makes it feel alive (not random, just drifting)
const phase = time * (0.6 + arousal * 1.2);

for (let i = 0; i < bufferLength; i++) {
  const t = i / (bufferLength - 1);     // 0..1
  const s = (timeData[i] - 128) / 128;  // -1..1

  // (A) Line scope coordinates (classic oscilloscope)
  const xLine = cx - coreRadius * 1.6 + t * (coreRadius * 3.2);   // width of the scope
  const yLine = cy + s * amp * 0.35;

  // (B) Loop coordinates (your existing ring)
  const ang = t * Math.PI * 2 + phase;
  const r = coreRadius + s * amp * 0.12;
  const xLoop = cx + Math.cos(ang) * r;
  const yLoop = cy + Math.sin(ang) * r;

  // Blend between line and loop
  const x = xLine * (1 - m) + xLoop * m;
  const y = yLine * (1 - m) + yLoop * m;

  if (i === 0) ctx.moveTo(x, y);
  else ctx.lineTo(x, y);
}

ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(255,255,255,${0.35 + 0.35 * m})`;
ctx.lineWidth = 2;
ctx.globalAlpha = 0.55 + 0.25 * bass;
ctx.setLineDash([]);
ctx.stroke();

